  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello!\nDESCRIPTION:\nI have a pair of sunglasses on my avatar that I can tilt up with PhysBones with the limit type Hinge.\nIn order to be aware of the state of the sunglasses, I have a HUD Icon appear whenever my sunglasses over my eyes to know when they're down. I accomplish this by using the _Angle parameter of the Immobile PhysBone it's on. When it's greater than .1 (aka, lifted), then the icon turns off. When it's less than, the icon turns on. I also have it so it turns off when I turn off the Sunglasses object.\nThe problem arises when I turn off the sunglasses toggle whenever they are up. The value of sgBone_Angle stays at whatever it was when I turned the toggle off.\nExpected behavior is to reset the Angle to 0 when the object is reactivated, because the object itself is back to the initial angle.\nBehavior seen is the _Angle stays at the value when the object was deactivated.\nSTEPS TO REPRODUCE:\n1. Have the physbone on a GameObject toggle. Set Immobile to 0, type Hinge. Give it a parameter (Example: Bone1\n2. Open debug menu. Observe Bone1_Angle parameter.\n3. Move the Bone1 physbone any amount, so that the Bone1_Angle is greater than 0.\n4. Toggle Bone1's gameobject off\n5. Observe Bone1_Angle as greater than 0\n6. Toggle Bone1's GameObject back on.\n7. Bone1_Angle is still greater than 0, even though Bone1 has been reset back to its initial transform.",
